  "prompt": "=== Chain-of-thought analysis prompt ===\nYou are a software requirements analyst preparing a UML state machine model.\n\nAnalyze the requirement and extract only the modeling facts needed for a state transition diagram. Keep the analysis concise and evidence-based.\n\nReturn the analysis using exactly these headings:\nStates:\nInitial state:\nFinal states:\nEvents or conditions:\nTransitions:\nMissing or ambiguous details:\n\nDo not write PlantUML in this step.\n\nRequirement:\nE Ticketing For Bus — Polished Requirement Specification\n\nFunctional Requirements\n1. The system shall allow a user to create a new account.\n2. The system shall validate the registration of a new user.\n3. The system shall allow the user to log in upon successful registration.\n4. The system shall provide options for logged-in users to check their ticket status.\n5. The system shall allow a user to book a ticket, which will be confirmed then make the payment.\n6. The system shall enable users to manage their account details such as editing or deleting them.\n7. The system shall log out the user after they complete any action.\n\n=== Chain-of-thought analysis response ===\nStates:\nLogged Out, Registration, Validating Registration, Logged In, Booking, Confirming Booking, Paying\n\nInitial state:\nLogged Out\n\nFinal states:\nNone (system remains in a state after actions)\n\nEvents or conditions:\nUser Registration Request, Registration Validation Success, Registration Validation Failure, Login Request, Successful Login, Ticket Status Check Request, Book Ticket Request, Booking Confirmation, Payment Completion, Account Management Request, Logout Request\n\nTransitions:\nLogged Out -> Registration (User Registration Request)\nRegistration -> Validating Registration (Registration Validation Success/Failure)\nValidating Registration -> Logged Out (Registration Validation Failure)\nValidating Registration -> Logged In (Registration Validation Success)\nLogged In -> Booking (Book Ticket Request)\nBooking -> Confirming Booking (Booking Confirmation)\nConfirming Booking -> Paying (Payment Completion)\nPaying -> Logged In (Payment Completion)\nLogged In -> Logged In (Ticket Status Check Request, Account Management Request)\nLogged In -> Logged Out (Logout Request)\n\nMissing or ambiguous details:\nSpecific account management actions (edit/delete details - need clarification).  Error handling during booking/payment is not detailed. The exact flow after a failed payment is unclear. The system's behavior after a user account is deleted is not specified.\n\n=== PlantUML generation prompt ===\nYou are a UML modeling expert.\n\nConvert the requirement and the structured analysis into one UML state transition diagram in PlantUML format.\n\nOutput Rules:\n- Generate ONLY valid PlantUML code.\n- Start with @startuml and end with @enduml.\n- Use [*] for exactly one initial transition.\n- Include at least one final transition to [*].\n- Use clear transition labels when requirement evidence exists.\n- Do not include explanations, analysis, or markdown fences.\n\nRequirement:\nE Ticketing For Bus — Polished Requirement Specification\n\nFunctional Requirements\n1. The system shall allow a user to create a new account.\n2. The system shall validate the registration of a new user.\n3. The system shall allow the user to log in upon successful registration.\n4. The system shall provide options for logged-in users to check their ticket status.\n5. The system shall allow a user to book a ticket, which will be confirmed then make the payment.\n6. The system shall enable users to manage their account details such as editing or deleting them.\n7. The system shall log out the user after they complete any action.\n\nStructured analysis from step 1:\nStates:\nLogged Out, Registration, Validating Registration, Logged In, Booking, Confirming Booking, Paying\n\nInitial state:\nLogged Out\n\nFinal states:\nNone (system remains in a state after actions)\n\nEvents or conditions